cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository, cite the relevant research preprint(s) listed in references/bibliography.md. This citation metadata describes the repository documentation, not the restricted datasets."
title: "Player Trust Research: Fairness Perception and Trust Erosion in Competitive Mobile Gaming"
authors:
  - family-names: "Hatefi Yousefi"
    given-names: "Hanieh"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-15"
abstract: >-
  Public-facing documentation for two related qualitative research studies
  examining player discourse about perceived fairness, manipulation, and trust
  in competitive mobile backgammon environments. The repository documents
  source-specific methods and findings while preserving client and product
  anonymity. It does not distribute raw datasets or grant an open reuse licence.
keywords:
  - UX research
  - player experience
  - digital trust
  - game research
  - qualitative research
  - thematic analysis
  - cross-cultural research
  - fairness perception
